    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "You’re about to go on a fantastic trip around Thailand. Great! Still, might be worried about how this will all cost you. Of course, we can’t put a definite number on it, but we can give you a good estimate. Below is an overview of all your potential travel expenses.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Step 1: Expenses before departure",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Below is an overview of average expenses before leaving for Thailand:",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "1. Plane tickets",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Price differences between return tickets to Bangkok can be huge. A general rule of thumb is: the sooner you book, the lower the price.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Other practical tips for booking a cheap flight:",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Direct flights are more expensive than flights with stops;",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Travel during low season (April to June & September and October);",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Also look for flights from nearby airports, as rates can be a lot cheaper;",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Search using comparison sites such as Skyscanner.",
            "url": "https://gotothailand.com/skyscanner",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://gotothailand.com/skyscanner",
                "anchor_text": "Skyscanner"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Take out a good (annual) travel insurance plan before leaving. Make sure you opt for worldwide coverage and take out extra insurance for medical costs. That way, should you need to be hospitalized while in Thailand, you’ll have sufficient coverage. You can choose to take out luggage insurance and cancellation insurance as well.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "2. Vaccinations",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "For most standard tourists there are no compulsory vaccinations for Thailand, though there are few recommended:",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Against childhood diseases: Tetanus and Diphtheria, Measles, Mumps, and Rubella.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Against food borne diseases: Typhoid and Hepatitis A.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Contact your local medical bureau for the fees.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "3. Visa",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Currently, passport holders of 57 countries are allowed to travel to Thailand without a visa, whether it’s by land or by air. This “visa-free entry” is free and is valid for a tourist stay of maximum 30 or 90 days. Click here for more information.",
            "url": "https://gotothailand.com/visa/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://gotothailand.com/visa/",
                "anchor_text": "Click here"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "If your country does not qualify for a visa-free entry, or if you wish to stay for a longer period, you could apply for a single entry visa (60 days) or multiple entry visa (3x 60 days). Click here for the application fees.",
            "url": "https://gotothailand.com/visa/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://gotothailand.com/visa/",
                "anchor_text": "Click here"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
