      {
        "h_title": "Low budget",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Traveling through Thailand and having a great time is possible, even on the smallest of budgets. Expect to pay ฿ 1,000 per day. You’ll be staying in clean, but basic, accommodations that you’ll share with other backpackers. Sleeping in a dorm is about 200 baht, or you can share a room with the person you’re traveling with.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Eat and drink with the locals: on the street. If you’re having dinner in a restaurant, order the cheaper Thai meals.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "When traveling by local bus or by train, travel in second class. Organize your own day trips; tours and excursions can be pretty expensive. But don’t worry. This is a great and adventurous way to explore Thailand. You’ll still have some money left to have some for a meal and a drink in the evening.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Average budget",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "You can easily get by on a budget of ฿ 2,000 (± $ 60) per day in Thailand. You’ll stay in clean, pleasant hotel rooms, all with their own unique flavor. Expect to pay about ฿ 1,000 (± $ 30) for a nice double room. You’ll be able to enjoy your fair share of luxury, mainly in the north of Thailand. The south is a lot more expensive, especially if you want to stay on the beach.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "You can easily afford to go out for food three times a day, but we would recommend everyone to have at least one street food meal a day. Street food is tasty, safe and cheap.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "You can visit fun sights every day and go on a couple of excursions a week. To get around you can take the tuk-tuk, hail a taxi, or travel in a comfortable air-conditioned bus or take a domestic flight.",
            "url": "https://gotothailand.com/thai-domestic-flights/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://gotothailand.com/thai-domestic-flights/",
                "anchor_text": "domestic flight"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "High budget",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Travelers who love luxury can enjoy all their heart’s desires in Thailand. The most luxurious resorts in Thailand happen to still be pretty affordable. You can book yourself a nice luxurious suite with a view of the Bangkok skyline or a really nice bungalow with a tropical beach view for anywhere between $ 100 and $ 250.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Go out for food three times a day, wherever you want. From authentic high-end restaurants to international cuisine, you can have it all, wherever and whenever you want.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Hire a chauffeur, buy a first class train ticket or fly business class to make your way around the country in comfort, or go on private party excursions. Why not rent a boat for few days? The sky is the limit!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Step 3: Final advice on budgets",
        "main_title": "Planning Your Travel Budget for Thailand",
        "author": "https://www.facebook.com/GoToThailand1/",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Take at least 500 USD or EUR banknotes with you to Thailand and exchange it there. It’s cheaper than using an ATM.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Bring sun cream and after sun with you. These things are a lot more expensive in Thailand.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Eat local food; it’s cheaper and a lot better as well.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Travel at night, by sleeper train for instance. This way, you’ll be traveling while sleeping and avoid paying for a hotel stay.",
            "url": "https://gotothailand.com/thai-sleeper-trains/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://gotothailand.com/thai-sleeper-trains/",
                "anchor_text": "sleeper train"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "And, last but not least, check out our blog post on 27 Tips to Save Money in Thailand.",
            "url": "https://gotothailand.com/save-money-tips-thailand/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://gotothailand.com/save-money-tips-thailand/",
                "anchor_text": "27 Tips to Save Money in Thailand"
              }
            ]
